From 0ae0766b440c3eae97f2eccd1e5a673bbb27ca73 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VCKing101 <59761021+VCKing101@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 00:37:05 +1030
Subject: [PATCH] Simulate-only frames and a restore that keeps real time, for
 rollback

Kernel::set_simulate_only (hle_extension::set_simulate_only): while on,
nothing waits for real time (the hold is neither slept on nor moved), the
flip presents nothing, display lists are walked as without a renderer, and
game audio reaches no device (the channels' times still count). A netplay
port turns it on for the frames it runs again after a restore and off when
the game is back at the frame it had reached. snapshot::restore and
Kernel::restore_state take keep_pacing, so those frames end where real time
already is instead of the hold starting again; snapshot::save_into reuses a
state's buffers, for a ring saved every frame.

Tested with Dissidia 012 on Windows: online battles between two copies on
one PC with 7 frames of rollback over a simulated 100 ms path kept full
speed and stayed in step. Not tested: other games, Linux, the Deck.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
